WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.999
A replacement candidate arrives with a green aggregate score.

2
00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:08.376
The operator sees improvement. The critic sees the same summary.

3
00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:13.190
Everyone is ready to approve—until one hidden cohort enters the denominator.

4
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:18.325
Inside that cohort are two unsafe releases. The aggregate score survives,

5
00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:22.859
but the replacement decision does not. Oversight helped only because it

6
00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:25.745
exposed a branch the original view concealed.

7
00:00:26.345 --> 00:00:30.340
That distinction is the chapter: a persuasive review process is not

8
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.972
the same thing as a correct result, and neither one

9
00:00:33.972 --> 00:00:35.425
supplies authority to act.

10
00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:40.685
Start with three asymmetries. Capability asks whether the supervisor can recognize

11
00:00:40.685 --> 00:00:45.346
a defect the stronger system can produce. Access asks whether the

12
00:00:45.346 --> 00:00:48.735
decisive evidence is visible. Authority asks who may

13
00:00:48.735 --> 00:00:50.430
make the downstream decision.

14
00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.530
Collapsing those questions into one review-quality score hides why a case

15
00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.985
should pass, narrow, escalate, or stop.

16
00:00:58.585 --> 00:01:03.588
Now freeze the request: task, risk tier, intended consumer, evidence views,

17
00:01:03.588 --> 00:01:08.590
turn and time budget, supervisor limits, system assumptions, and stop condition.

18
00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.681
Only then choose a route: direct review, consultation, adversarial review,

19
00:01:13.681 --> 00:01:17.723
or abstention. The route is conditional on the task;

20
00:01:17.723 --> 00:01:19.520
no protocol wins everywhere.

21
00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.531
Return to the candidate. The proposer can inspect per-cohort results and

22
00:01:24.531 --> 00:01:28.141
training lineage. The critic initially sees only the summary.

23
00:01:28.141 --> 00:01:31.750
Different role labels do not repair that access mismatch.

24
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.852
The evidence view is repaired with the frozen cohort manifest,

25
00:01:36.852 --> 00:01:41.804
exact candidate digest, and regression artifacts. Now the critic can inspect

26
00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:45.405
the same decisive branch—but independence is still unresolved.

27
00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:50.386
Both models share a base family, retrieval corpus, and tool chain.

28
00:01:50.386 --> 00:01:54.767
A dependency graph shows three common edges. Two voices can therefore

29
00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.360
fail as one system.

30
00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.970
The proposer and critic precommit to opposite claims.

31
00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.979
Their transcript is useful as a search process,

32
00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:06.365
but winning the exchange is not the outcome reference.

33
00:02:06.965 --> 00:02:11.886
An independently routed auditor replays the missing cohort and finds the

34
00:02:11.886 --> 00:02:15.913
two unsafe releases. The audit establishes a bounded defect;

35
00:02:15.913 --> 00:02:19.045
it does not establish universal auditor competence.

36
00:02:19.645 --> 00:02:24.332
Compare the assisted path with an informed direct-review baseline under the

37
00:02:24.332 --> 00:02:29.019
same evidence, time, and cost envelope. A protocol deserves credit only

38
00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:31.575
for improvement over that real comparator.

39
00:02:32.175 --> 00:02:36.710
The receipt now separates four achievements: the critic exposes a defect,

40
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:40.420
the auditor verifies it, the evidence layer records it,

41
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:44.955
and the authority holder blocks replacement. None may impersonate the next.

42
00:02:45.555 --> 00:02:50.966
So the candidate routes to quarantine. The aggregate score, omitted cohort,

43
00:02:50.966 --> 00:02:54.901
unsafe outcomes, shared-family residual, operator time, model calls,

44
00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.360
and rerun requirement remain attached.

45
00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:02.709
If the auditor were missing, the same transcript would route to

46
00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:06.163
accountable escalation—not an inferred pass. Honest incompleteness is

47
00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:07.890
a valid controlled outcome.

48
00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:14.646
The protocol receipt binds task cohort, capability and access envelopes, roles,

49
00:03:14.646 --> 00:03:19.683
incentives, dependency graph, direct baseline, outcome audit, calibration, coverage,

50
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:22.481
abstention, residual owner, permitted consumer,

51
00:03:22.481 --> 00:03:24.720
expiry, and requalification triggers.

52
00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.129
Consumer binding matters. A claim-review aid cannot silently become a training

53
00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:34.500
label, and a low-risk receipt cannot silently become release permission.

54
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:40.206
Material changes reopen admission: model, task distribution, evidence view, prompt,

55
00:03:40.206 --> 00:03:45.312
retrieval corpus, judge, protocol, or auditor. Unchanged bytes do not

56
00:03:45.312 --> 00:03:47.355
mean an unchanged intervention.

57
00:03:47.955 --> 00:03:53.044
Abstention also needs evidence. Record the unresolved proposition, what was tried,

58
00:03:53.044 --> 00:03:58.134
which budget ended, the defeater, queue effect, and next escalation route.

59
00:03:58.134 --> 00:04:00.910
Generic refusal earns no safety credit.

60
00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:07.139
Four failure patterns remain visible. Persuasion theater rewards the best advocate.

61
00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:11.233
Correlated panels manufacture agreement. Weak baselines launder benefit.

62
00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:14.815
Selected cohorts hide the cases that matter.

63
00:04:15.415 --> 00:04:18.651
And scale can break the human path itself.

64
00:04:18.651 --> 00:04:23.100
More critics may increase discovery while also increasing latency, privacy exposure,

65
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.145
cost, fatigue, and the queue that owns the hard cases.

66
00:04:27.745 --> 00:04:32.613
Report the bundle together: useful throughput, unsafe admission, false rejection,

67
00:04:32.613 --> 00:04:36.507
coverage, selective risk, latency, operator burden, escalation load,

68
00:04:36.507 --> 00:04:41.375
and residual risk. No average may hide a failed control.

69
00:04:41.975 --> 00:04:46.266
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support.

70
00:04:46.266 --> 00:04:51.093
Its seven-stage lifecycle, fifty-eight routes, and sixty-five rejecting mutations

71
00:04:51.093 --> 00:04:55.384
test record custody and refusal semantics—not real reviewer

72
00:04:55.384 --> 00:04:57.530
competence or protocol value.

73
00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:03.215
No model, human study, natural workload, held-out outcome campaign, causal ablation,

74
00:05:03.215 --> 00:05:06.451
deployment, reproduction, or transfer has run here.

75
00:05:06.451 --> 00:05:10.611
The strongest warranted statement is that the proposed boundary

76
00:05:10.611 --> 00:05:12.460
is explicit and testable.

77
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.284
The payoff is a control plane, not an automated jury:

78
00:05:17.284 --> 00:05:21.086
assistance can make difficult work more inspectable while uncertainty,

79
00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:24.465
consumer scope, and authority remain separate and owned.

80
00:05:25.065 --> 00:05:29.756
Next, Human Intent as a Formal Input asks what the principal

81
00:05:29.756 --> 00:05:34.020
actually authorized before any reviewer or system interprets the request.
